# No default UI explainers

Ship **self-explanatory** UI. Do **not** add lead paragraphs, hint lines, or “what this does” blurbs under headings, toggles, or buttons by default.

## Do

- Rely on clear **titles**, **labels**, **button text**, and **empty states**.
- When tip / disclaimer / trademark copy is required (destructive, irreversible, security-critical, or legal), put it in **`InfoTip`** (`src/components/ui/InfoTip.svelte`) next to the control — not a hard-coded paragraph under it.
- Prefer tightening layout and naming over adding an explainer.

## Do not

- Default every new Settings (or similar) section to a muted sentence under the `h2`/`h3`.
- Restate the heading (“Preferred network” + “Default network for…”) or narrate product architecture in the UI.
- Add per-toggle/per-button description paragraphs that only rephrase the control label.
- Pad vertical space with explainer blocks “for clarity.”
- Ship tip copy as always-visible muted paragraphs when an `InfoTip` hover would suffice.

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<h2>Tokens to track</h2>
<p class="hint">Tracked assets appear in Send and in the DM wallet sidebar.</p>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<h2>Tokens to track</h2>
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — tip as hard-coded block -->
<label><input type="checkbox" /> Route Traffic Through Tor</label>
<p class="hint">Tor and the Tor logo are trademarks…</p>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<label><input type="checkbox" /> Route Traffic Through Tor</label>
<InfoTip text={$t('settings.routeTrafficThroughTorDisclaimer')} ariaLabel={…} />
```

If something is unclear after shipping, add a targeted `InfoTip` later — never as the default for every feature.
